{
 "about": {
  "title": "Grey wolf (Canis lupus tundrarum) skull, Mech 1974 Mammalian Species 37 Figure 5 (after Bee and Hall 1956:169): digitised side and dorsal outlines and landmarks",
  "source": "Mech, L. D. 1974. Canis lupus. Mammalian Species 37:1-6, Figure 5, page 4. https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/usgsnpwrc/334 (landing page: \"Comments: U.S. government work\"); PDF page 1 notice: \"This document is a U.S. government work and is not subject to copyright in the United States.\"",
  "figure_origin": "Figure 5 is captioned \"after Bee and Hall, 1956:169\" (Mammals of Northern Alaska, Univ. Kansas Mus. Nat. Hist. Misc. Publ. 8). The drawing is a redrawn copy published in a US government work; the underlying 1956 drawing is a University of Kansas publication (renewal not checked). Treat as public domain as published in Mech 1974, with the Bee and Hall caveat noted for a human.",
  "specimen": "C. l. tundrarum, Wahoo Lake, Alaska; sex and size not given; no scale bar, so all values are in fractions of condylobasal length (CBL), not mm",
  "date": "2026-10-07",
  "method": "page 4 rendered at 600 dpi (pdftoppm), lateral and dorsal views cropped, ink thresholded (<160), closed with a 4 px disk, holes filled, largest regions = skull and mandible; outer contour traced (skimage find_contours) and simplified at 2.5 px (0.0015 CBL). Landmarks placed by eye on gridded 600 dpi crops (A = silhouette extreme, B = clear structure, C = interpretation of the drawing).",
  "frame_side_2d": "same convention as ref/research/missingfound/wolf-skull: facing RIGHT (the drawing faces left and is mirrored), image y DOWN, origin = prosthion, X = forward +, Y = down +, units = CBL. CBL = horizontal distance prosthion to caudal-most occipital condyle = 1687 px at 600 dpi. The drawing horizontal is kept: the condyle then sits 3.05 deg above the prosthion level, matching the palate frame of the 3D skulls (170753: condyle Y = -0.053 CBL), so no rotation was applied.",
  "frame_mandible": "the mandible is drawn separately (not articulated). mandible_side_own_frame: origin = infradentale, facing right, y down, CBL units of the skull drawing. To articulate, translate so condyle_centre_EST sits on the hinge (use the 3D hinge (-0.754, -0.033) CBL from missingfound/wolf-skull, or tmj_glenoid_EST below).",
  "frame_dorsal_2d": "dorsal view facing right, y down, origin X = prosthion, Y = midline; scaled so its incisor-tip-to-inion length equals the lateral one (the dorsal drawing is 1.9 % larger than the lateral). Side of the animal is ambiguous (symmetric drawing).",
  "pixel_frame": "px values are in crops of page 4 rendered at 600 dpi: lateral crop origin (300, 2480), dorsal crop origin (300, 470). The stored file mech1974_fig5_skull_views_600dpi.png is the crop from (300, 460): add 2020 px to lateral y and 10 px to dorsal y to locate points in it (x unchanged)."
 },
